{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"InMemoryDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Deliver to it beside the destinations that send events away, then read what arrived: an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in-app event inspector or debug drawer listing what was just tracked, a recent-activity view,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a SwiftUI preview fed sample events, or a test checking what its code tracked.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let destination = InMemoryDestination(capacity: 500)","let tracker = Tracker()","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: destination).execute()","destination.events(of: SignedUp.self)  \/\/ [SignedUp(plan: \"pro\")]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It keeps at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" records, across batches: once a batch takes it past that, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"oldest records are dropped until the newest "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" remain. A batch some of whose records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"were dropped is kept with the newest of them, so "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination\/batches"},{"type":"text","text":" always holds "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination\/records"},{"type":"text","text":", in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination\/unbounded()"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps everything, for a run whose length the caller controls."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Copies share what they keep: the copy the delivery holds and the one the app reads are the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same log. Reading is safe from any thread while batches arrive.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Destinations"}],"externalID":"s:12Destinations19InMemoryDestinationV","title":"InMemoryDestination","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"InMemoryDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"InMemoryDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination.swift#L27","fileName":"InMemoryDestination.swift"}},"abstract":[{"text":"A destination that keeps the newest records it receives, in memory, for the app to read.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination\/init(capacity:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination\/init(checkedCapacity:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination\/batches","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination\/deliveries","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Dest